from mkchar import mk
mk("Callum_Morse.md","Callum Morse","2","Book 2","Book 13","Books 2, 3, 6, 8-11, 13 (chapter files)","Arabelle_Remore.md, Gabriel_Remore.md, Emir_Bahadir.md, Sophie_Wexler.md, Melody_Jain.md",
"A gold-rank stealth assassin, former teammate of Emir and of Rufus's parents, whose long hunt for Sophie's mother Melody Jain drives his later scenes.",
["Introduced by Emir as a gold-ranker who, if he does not want to be seen, cannot be seen by anyone short of diamond rank (Book 2, Ch34 L91).",
 "Described as \"the gold-ranked assassination specialist\" and the group's best scout (Book 2, Ch76 L7); his attacks on a gold-rank priest land strongly but do not kill at once (Book 2, Ch76 L41).",
 "He, Gabriel and Arabelle Remore have been companions for decades (Book 2, Ch76 L40). Emir, Arabelle, Gabriel and Callum were an old team (Book 3, Ch24 L35; Book 8, Ch27 L26).",
 "An avid monster-hunter, he is one of the few gold-rankers who obsessively raise their strength (Book 6, Ch47 L495).",
 "He stops Sophie and Humphrey from running off after the Order of the Reaper: \"I'm stopping you until you are ready. Hate me if you like\" (Book 6, Ch47 L581), and explains the order split from the cult and became self-serving assassins (Book 6, Ch47 L592).",
 "His fixation on Melody Jain, Sophie's mother, is because he is connected to her: she kept him as her only real connection to the order (Book 9, Ch27 L63); he lost track of her and has searched ever since (Book 9, Ch27 L91).",
 "Jason avoids his petitions to see Melody, and finds his aura dangerously unstable even after things are in the open (Book 8, Ch63 L140; Book 10, Ch58 L7).",
 "In Book 13 he conjures rats to track a creature through a pipe (Book 13, Ch958 L75)."],
"Quiet, patient and unfazed; he lets a hard decision stand and speaks plainly (\"Sensible\", Book 2, Ch36 L79). His grief and fixation on Melody are the one place his calm slips.",
timeline=["Book 2: scouts for the strike on the Builder cult's island (Book 2, Ch76 L7-46).","Book 3: reports on the cultists' escape and the Purity evidence (Book 3, Ch1 L77-82).","Book 6: stops Sophie and Humphrey in Kurdansk (Book 6, Ch47 L521-592).","Books 8-10: petitions Jason to see Melody (Book 8, Ch63 L140; Book 10, Ch58 L7).","Book 13: part of the expedition (Book 13, Ch958 L75)."])
mk("Valdis_Volaire.md","Valdis Volaire","1","Book 2","Book 12","Books 2, 3, 5, 12 (chapter files)","Clive_Standish.md, Humphrey_Geller.md, Jason_Asano.md",
"A swordmaster prince of the Kingdom of Mirrors whom Clive meets in the City of Fallen Echoes; he is cheerful, reckless and a rival and friend to Jason's team.",
["Introduces himself as \"Valdis\" and praises Clive's reputation (Book 2, Ch48 L77); the system names him Valdis Volaire (Book 2, Ch51 L56).",
 "A prince of the small but influential Kingdom of Mirrors, whose borders have not changed in eight centuries (Book 2, Ch51 L8); his father, the Mirror King, is eight hundred years old and the kingdom is \"thick with princes and princesses\" (Book 2, Ch55 L63; Book 12, Ch15 L9).",
 "A reckless enthusiast who leads his three teammates up a tower in search of treasure (Book 2, Ch51 L9-10); he has a light-step power, a slow-fall power and a wall run (Book 2, Ch51 L17, L28, L32).",
 "He chooses the path of courage in the trial and is the first to step forward (Book 2, Ch51 L42; Book 2, Ch57 L63).",
 "A sword master, mobile striker and the stronger team's leader (Book 3, Ch4 L3, L7); his team is a highly efficient cohort trained since before they had essences (Book 3, Ch3 L80).",
 "His father collects him from Jason's ship, to Valdis's embarrassment (Book 3, Ch5 L42-50); he portals in for Jason's memorial (Book 3, Ch69 L895).",
 "By Book 12 he is Sigrid's husband (Book 12, Ch15 L8), assembles an arena event in under two days (Book 12, Ch16 L11), and fights Jason in a mirage chamber using Mind's Eye to sense the space around him (Book 12, Ch17 L55-73)."],
"Boisterous, flirtatious and fond of a good story (\"the virile verve of ten men\", Book 2, Ch61 L74); he loves duelling famous warriors for the push, not the win (Book 12, Ch17 L56).",
timeline=["Book 2: Clive's team-mate in the City of Fallen Echoes; party and trials (Book 2, Ch48-61).","Book 3: friendly rival team; mock battles (Book 3, Ch4; Book 5, Ch64 L24).","Book 12: Mirror Kingdom arena duel with Jason (Book 12, Ch15-17)."])
